$ Python standard library: ssl.SSLSocket
@ ssl.SSLSocket

The class `ssl.SSLSocket is derived from `→ development/languages/Python/standard-library/socket[socket].socket` and wraps the underlying
OS socket in an → development/security/cryptography/SSL-TLS[SSL] context when necessary, and provides read and write method over that channel.

`SSLSocket` isntances must be created with `ssl_context.wrap_socket()` (where `ssl_context` is an instance of `ssl.SSLContext`).

